# Persian AI Assistant - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
This is a Persian AI Assistant project featuring a React/TypeScript frontend and Go backend, providing AI chat capabilities, image generation, translation services, and Persian language support with RTL layout.

## Core Technologies & Dependencies

### Frontend Stack
- **Framework**: React 18+ with TypeScript 5.8+
- **Build Tool**: Vite 6.2+ with Bun runtime
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.1+ with shadcn/ui components
- **State Management**: Jotai for atomic state, TanStack Query for server state
- **Routing**: React Router DOM 7.4+
- **Font**: Vazirmatn for Persian text support
- **UI Components**: Radix UI primitives with custom shadcn/ui components

### Backend Stack
- **Language**: Go 1.24+
- **Framework**: Echo 4.13+ for HTTP handling
- **Database**: SQLite with GORM ORM
- **Logging**: Zerolog with Lumberjack for rotation
- **Hot Reload**: Air for development
- **Documentation**: Swagger/OpenAPI 3.0

### External Services
- **AI Models**: Ollama (port 11434) for local AI inference
- **Image Generation**: Stable Diffusion (port 7860)
- **Speech-to-Text**: Whisper integration

## Code Style & Conventions

### TypeScript/React Frontend

#### File & Component Naming
- **Components**: PascalCase with `.tsx` extension (`Message.tsx`, `ChatInput.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: camelCase with `.ts` extension (`utils.ts`, `atoms.ts`)
- **Hooks**: camelCase starting with `use` (`useGetDefaultChatModel`)
- **Constants**: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (`DEFAULT_CHAT_MODEL_STORAGE_KEY`)

#### Component Structure
```tsx
// Use interface for props
export interface MessageProps {
  message: MessageType;
}

// Functional components with explicit typing
export function Message({ message }: MessageProps) {
  // Component implementation
}
```

#### State Management Patterns
- Use Jotai atoms for global state with custom hooks
- Prefix storage keys with descriptive names
- Combine localStorage with atoms for persistence
```tsx
export const useSetDefaultChatModel = () => {
  const setDefaultChatModel = useSetAtom(defaultChatModelAtom);
  
  return (model: string) => {
    localStorage.setItem(DEFAULT_CHAT_MODEL_STORAGE_KEY, model);
    setDefaultChatModel(model);
  };
};
```

#### Styling Conventions
- Use `cn()` utility function for combining Tailwind classes
- Implement RTL/LTR detection with `detectTextDirection()`
- Apply dark mode variants consistently
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes, avoid custom CSS when possible
- Organizing classes is done via prettier-tailwindcss plugin

#### Import Organization
```tsx
// External libraries
import { useState } from "react";
import ReactMarkdown from "react-markdown";

// Internal components
import { Button } from "@/components/ui";
import type { DbMessage as MessageType } from "../../generated/apiSchemas";

// Utilities and constants
import { PERSIAN_TEXTS } from "@/lib/persian-texts";
import { cn, detectTextDirection } from "@/lib/utils";
```

### Go Backend

#### File & Package Structure
- **Handlers**: Organize by feature (`chat.go`, `translate.go`)
- **Types**: Define in `types.go` within relevant packages
- **Database**: Separate models in `db/models.go`
- **Utilities**: Helper functions in `utils/` directory

#### Code Conventions
- Use structured logging with zerolog
- Implement proper error handling with context
- Follow Go standard package organization
- Use middleware for cross-cutting concerns

#### Handler Pattern
```go
type Handler struct {
    db           *gorm.DB
    ollamaClient *api.Client
}

func NewHandler(db *gorm.DB, ollamaClient *api.Client) *Handler {
    return &Handler{
        db:           db,
        ollamaClient: ollamaClient,
    }
}
```

#### Logging Standards
```go
log.Info().
    Str("method", v.Method).
    Str("uri", v.URI).
    Int("status", v.Status).
    Msg("Request handled")
```

## Project Structure Guidelines

### Frontend Directory Structure
```
src/
├── components/          # Reusable UI components
│   ├── layouts/        # Layout components
│   ├── ui/             # Base UI components (shadcn/ui)
│   └── translation/    # Feature-specific components
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
├── lib/                # Utilities & configurations
│   ├── api/           # API integration utilities
│   └── utils.ts       # Helper functions
├── pages/              # Route components
├── services/           # External service integrations
├── atoms.ts            # Global state management
└── app.tsx             # Main application setup
```

### Backend Directory Structure
```
backend/
├── handlers/           # HTTP request handlers
├── db/                 # Database operations & models
├── docs/               # API documentation
├── logger/             # Custom logging implementation
├── utils/              # Helper functions
└── main.go             # Server entry point
```

## Development Workflow

### Build & Development Commands
- `make install` - Install all dependencies
- `make dev` - Start both frontend and backend in development mode
- `make build` - Build production-ready application
- `make generate-types` - Generate TypeScript types from Go API

### Code Quality
- **Frontend**: ESLint + Prettier with Tailwind plugin
- **Backend**: Standard Go formatting with gofmt
- **Type Safety**: Strict TypeScript configuration
- **API Types**: Auto-generated from OpenAPI specs

## Persian Language & RTL Support

### Text Direction Handling
- Detect text direction automatically using `detectTextDirection()`
- Apply `dir="rtl"` or `dir="ltr"` attributes dynamically
- Use RTL-aware Tailwind classes (`rtl:`, `ltr:`)

### Font & Typography
- Primary font: Vazirmatn variable font for Persian text
- Ensure proper Persian character rendering
- Support mixed LTR/RTL content in chat messages

## API Design Patterns

### Response Structures
```typescript
interface Response<T> {
  data: T;
}

interface PaginatedResponse<T> {
  data: T[];
  has_next: boolean;
  total: number;
  current_page: number;
}
```

### Streaming Responses
- Use Server-Sent Events for real-time chat responses
- Implement proper error handling in streams
- Support abortable requests with AbortController

## Database Conventions

### Model Relationships
- Use GORM associations for related data
- Implement soft deletes where appropriate
- Include timestamps (CreatedAt, UpdatedAt)

### Schema Design
```go
type ChatThread struct {
    ID       uint      `gorm:"primaryKey"`
    Title    string    
    Messages []Message `gorm:"foreignKey:ChatThreadID"`
    Model    string    
    CreatedAt time.Time
    UpdatedAt time.Time
}
```

## Security & Privacy
- All AI processing happens locally (Ollama, Stable Diffusion)
- No external API calls for sensitive data
- Proper CORS configuration for development
- Structured logging without sensitive data exposure

## Error Handling

### Frontend
- Use TanStack Query for API error handling
- Implement loading states and error boundaries
- Provide user-friendly error messages in Persian

### Backend
- Structured error responses with proper HTTP status codes
- Comprehensive logging with context
- Graceful degradation for external service failures

## Performance Considerations

### Frontend
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement proper loading states
- Optimize bundle size with dynamic imports

### Backend
- Connection pooling for database
- Proper middleware ordering
- Streaming responses for long-running operations

## Testing Guidelines

### Frontend
- Component testing with React Testing Library
- Type checking with TypeScript compiler
- ESLint for code quality

### Backend
- Unit tests for handlers and utilities
- Integration tests for API endpoints
- Database migration testing

## Deployment & Build

### Environment Configuration
- Use `.env` files for configuration
- Separate development and production configs
- Embed static files in Go binary for distribution

### Build Process
- Frontend: Vite build with TypeScript checking
- Backend: Go build with embedded static files
- Single binary deployment target

## Documentation Standards

### Code Documentation
- JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Go doc comments for exported functions
- README sections for major features

### API Documentation
- OpenAPI 3.0 specifications
- Auto-generated TypeScript types
- Swagger UI for development

Remember to maintain consistency with these patterns and always consider Persian language support and RTL layout requirements when implementing new features. 